# Frontend design

Read `DESIGN.md` before writing or changing any UI. Implement it; do not invent a parallel look.

Non-negotiables:

- One accent: `{colors.primary}` `#0066cc`. Dark-tile links use `{colors.primary-on-dark}` `#2997ff` only.
- No second brand color. No decorative gradients. No card/button/text shadows.
- The only drop-shadow is `rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.22) 3px 5px 30px` on product imagery.
- Body is 17px / 400 / 1.47. Headlines are 600 with negative letter-spacing. No weight 500.
- Primary actions are `{rounded.pill}` blue pills. Press = `transform: scale(0.95)`.
- Sections are full-bleed tiles. Alternate white/parchment and near-black; the color change is the divider.
- Map UI to named components in `DESIGN.md` (`global-nav`, `product-tile-*`, `button-primary`, `store-utility-card`).
- Use design tokens, not ad-hoc hex/radius/type.

If a screen is not specified, pick the closest component in `DESIGN.md` and stay inside its tokens.
